From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: waydroid-nvidia-prolapse <build@local>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:58:44 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/20] hwcomposer: never shrink the HIDL thread pool from the
 binder thread

What: hwc_binder_thread() configures the HIDL pool with
max(1, hardware::ProcessState::self()->getMaxThreads()) threads instead of 1.

Why: the composer service (hardware/interfaces graphics/composer/2.1/default/
service.cpp at the pinned AOSP commit) calls configureRpcThreadpool(4, true),
then HwcLoader::load() (which opens this module; hwc_open() starts
hwc_binder_thread), then composer->registerAsService(). Registration runs
hidl-gen's BpHwServiceManager::_hidl_add*, which call
hardware::ProcessState::startThreadPool() (the image's libhidlbase has 14 such
call sites, objdump). libhwbinder ProcessState::setThreadPoolConfiguration()
(pinned system/libhwbinder ProcessState.cpp:311) is
LOG_ALWAYS_FATAL_IF(mThreadPoolStarted && maxThreads < mMaxThreads,
"Binder threadpool cannot be shrunk after starting"). So when the main
thread's registration wins the race against this thread's
configureRpcThreadpool(1, true), 1 < 4 aborts the composer at start, and
SurfaceFlinger and zygote restart behind it. Not seen in this project's
retained logs (50 tombstones, 58 dropbox tombstones: no composer crash), but
the path is reachable on every start. The configured count is written by
main before this thread exists and startThreadPool() does not change it, so
re-using it is never a shrink, whichever thread wins.

Source: problem reported by QuinOvaX, quinovax/waydroid-nvidia dev 74f7b93
  https://github.com/quinovax/waydroid-nvidia/commit/74f7b9308fa1d1e4e81fb52570735ed562ee3fc1
  (observed there as two composer aborts at start, 2026-10-04).
Licence: Apache-2.0 (android_hardware_waydroid).

Deviation from the source: the fix is ours. The source replaced
configure/join with setupBinderPolling()/handleBinderPoll(), but
IPCThreadState::setupPolling() itself calls
setThreadPoolConfiguration(1, true) (pinned libhwbinder IPCThreadState.cpp:579),
the same guard, and its handleBinderPoll() loop never poll()s the fd. It also
cites ProcessState.cpp:393, which is libbinder's (frameworks/native) copy of
the guard; HIDL's configureRpcThreadpool goes to libhwbinder.
---
 hwcomposer/hwcomposer.cpp | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hwcomposer/hwcomposer.cpp b/hwcomposer/hwcomposer.cpp
index 4bb6a18..80ad7e6 100644
--- a/hwcomposer/hwcomposer.cpp
+++ b/hwcomposer/hwcomposer.cpp
@@ -17,6 +17,9 @@
 
 #include "hwcomposer.h"
 
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <hwbinder/ProcessState.h>
+
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <pthread.h>
 #include <semaphore.h>
@@ -789,7 +792,18 @@ static void* hwc_binder_thread(void* data) {
     sp<IWaydroidClipboard> waydroidClipboard;
 
     setpriority(PRIO_PROCESS, 0, HAL_PRIORITY_URGENT_DISPLAY);
-    configureRpcThreadpool(1, true /*callerWillJoin*/);
+    /* Never shrink the HIDL thread pool. This module is loaded by
+     * android.hardware.graphics.composer@2.1-service, whose main() has already called
+     * configureRpcThreadpool(4, true) before HwcLoader::load() opened us, and whose
+     * registerAsService() (hidl-gen BpHwServiceManager::_hidl_add*, run concurrently with this
+     * thread) calls hardware::ProcessState::startThreadPool(). libhwbinder's
+     * setThreadPoolConfiguration() is LOG_ALWAYS_FATAL when the pool is started and the new
+     * count is lower ("Binder threadpool cannot be shrunk after starting"), so the old
+     * configureRpcThreadpool(1, true) aborted the composer whenever main won that race.
+     * Re-using the configured count (main's configure happens-before this thread exists) can
+     * never be lower, whatever the order; a process with no configured pool gets 1 as before. */
+    configureRpcThreadpool(std::max<size_t>(1, android::hardware::ProcessState::self()->getMaxThreads()),
+                           true /*callerWillJoin*/);
 
     waydroidDisplay = new WaydroidDisplay(pdev->display);
     if (waydroidDisplay == nullptr) {
